cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "les-kinetic-reduction-lab: how much chemistry does a reacting-flow LES need?"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
license: MIT
authors:
  - given-names: "Mintesinot"
    family-names: "Alemayehu Akale"
    affiliation: "Bahir Dar Institute of Technology, Bahir Dar University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/les-kinetic-reduction-lab"
abstract: >-
  A self-contained teaching project that takes a chain-branching kinetic
  mechanism from detailed to skeletal (DRGEP) to global one-step, and measures
  the accuracy and cost of each level in a 2D large-eddy simulation of an
  auto-igniting jet. Pure Python (NumPy/SciPy/Matplotlib).
keywords:
  - combustion
  - chemical kinetics
  - mechanism reduction
  - DRGEP
  - large-eddy simulation
  - reacting flows
